- Initially after A1 processed, tip A1. Then B1 processed. A1 vs B1: A1 heavier. Then B2 added; B2's branch total blue_work > A1. Selected becomes B2, chain = Tb, B1, B2. In that chain, retiro applied once via B1.
- Check: exactly one en_retirada entry with importe, nonce_siguiente = n+1. Also the same tx object in A1.
- Then add A2, A3 (heavier) to reorg back to A: A2 (sr=0), A3 (sr=0). Selected chain A: Tb, A1, A2, A3. Retiro applied once.
This tests repetition across reorg: the same operation appears in both branches and is applied exactly once in whichever chain is selected. Good.

